Q: How to set variables in GitHub workflows/actions in VS Code? A: <pre><code>&lt;Tabs
  screenOptions={{
    header: (props) =&gt; &lt;CustomHeader {...props} /&gt;,
    headerStyle: { height: 100 },
  }}
  sceneContainerStyle={{
    paddingHorizontal: 16,
    paddingVertical: 12,
  }}
&gt;
  &lt;Tabs.Screen name=&quot;index&quot; /&gt;
  &lt;Tabs.Screen name=&quot;profile&quot; /&gt;
  {/* all screens get the padding automatically */}
&lt;/Tabs&gt;
</code></pre>

Q: Eslint warning for dangerous use of &quot;as&quot; A: <h1><a href="https://typescript-eslint.io/rules/no-unsafe-type-assertion/" rel="nofollow noreferrer">no-unsafe-type-assertion</a></h1>
<blockquote>
<p>This rule forbids using type assertions to narrow a type, as this bypasses TypeScript's type-checking. Type assertions that broaden a type are safe because TypeScript essentially knows <em>less</em> about a type.</p>
</blockquote>
<pre class="lang-mjs prettyprint-override"><code>export default defineConfig({
  rules: {
    &quot;@typescript-eslint/no-unsafe-type-assertion&quot;: &quot;error&quot;
  }
});
</code></pre>
